---
title: "About Lesli — Why We Built a Modular Rails Framework"
description: "Learn why Lesli exists, the principles behind it, who it is for, and how it helps teams build software they can own and evolve."
---

<header class="about-header">
    <%= partial("partials/lesli-navigation", locals: { logo: true }) %>

    <div class="container about-hero">
        <p class="about-eyebrow">About Lesli</p>
        <h1>A better foundation for teams <span class="lesli-title-colored">building software for the long term.</span></h1>
        <p class="about-introduction">
            Lesli exists so teams can spend less time rebuilding common application infrastructure and more time
            creating the workflows, experiences, and value that make their product different.
        </p>

        <ul class="about-pillars" aria-label="Principles behind Lesli">
            <li class="about-pillar about-pillar--open">
                <span class="about-pillar-icon ri-open-source-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <strong>Open source by default</strong>
                <span>Use, inspect, adapt, and contribute to Lesli under the GPLv3 license.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="about-pillar about-pillar--rails">
                <span class="about-pillar-icon ri-code-box-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <strong>Rails-native</strong>
                <span>Work with standard Rails applications, engines, conventions, and tools.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="about-pillar about-pillar--ownership">
                <span class="about-pillar-icon ri-box-3-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <strong>Built to be owned</strong>
                <span>Your code, data, workflows, integrations, and roadmap remain yours.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</header>

<main class="about-content">
    <section class="about-purpose">
        <div class="container">
            <p class="about-section-label">Why Lesli exists</p>
            <h2>Build the product—not the same foundation again.</h2>
            <div class="about-purpose-copy">
                <p>
                    Business software repeatedly needs accounts, users, permissions, navigation, auditing,
                    notifications, shared interface patterns, and other essential capabilities.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Lesli turns those repeatable concerns into a shared foundation and modular capabilities, so teams
                    can focus on the business model, workflows, and customer experience that make each product unique.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-editorial">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="about-editorial-grid">
                <article>
                    <p class="about-section-label">Who it is for</p>
                    <h2>Teams building software that will evolve.</h2>
                    <p>
                        Lesli fits multi-account SaaS products, internal operations platforms, customer portals,
                        workflow applications, and custom business systems—especially when roles, domains,
                        integrations, and history grow over time.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <p class="about-section-label">What it is—and isn't</p>
                    <h2>A framework, not a finished product.</h2>
                    <p>
                        Lesli is not a hosted service, no-code builder, admin template, or one-time boilerplate. It is
                        installed in a Rails application, where you choose official or custom modules and shape them
                        around the product you need to build.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-closing">
        <div class="container">
            <p class="about-section-label">The idea</p>
            <h2>Start with structure. Keep control.</h2>
            <p>Use the foundation, add only what your product needs, and keep ownership of what you build.</p>
            <div class="about-actions">
                <a class="button-primary" href="/#how-lesli-works">
                    See how Lesli works
                    <span class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </a>
                <a class="button-primary-ghost" href="/engines/lesli/about/architecture/">
                    Explore the architecture
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
